{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-98186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate \n${\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)+⟨-1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{3}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨5,\\,-1,\\,-2⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/state.json" "file_sha256" "78c771458bf0af71173b6ade2cf888be688e0da9d2268b37961ea4c3b98b979c"} {"question" "q-98186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{3}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨5,\\,-1,\\,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-5,\\,1,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the vector addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)+⟨-1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{3}⟨-1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨-5,\\,1,\\,2⟩+{⟨-t,\\,t,\\,-t⟩|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =⟨-5,\\,1,\\,2⟩+⟨-3,\\,3,\\,-3⟩\\text{ } \\\\  & =⟨-8,\\,4,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/state.json" "file_sha256" "78c771458bf0af71173b6ade2cf888be688e0da9d2268b37961ea4c3b98b979c"} {"question" "q-98186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "be742f513a141cf803ea569247221f898bdc03e6301fb9cba23ca22ad4c28ba0"} {"question" "q-98186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/state.json" "file_sha256" "78c771458bf0af71173b6ade2cf888be688e0da9d2268b37961ea4c3b98b979c"} {"question" "q-98186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-8,\\,2,\\,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨-8,\\,4,\\,-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,\\,-2,\\,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,\\,2,\\,-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨8,\\,4,\\,1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/state.json" "file_sha256" "78c771458bf0af71173b6ade2cf888be688e0da9d2268b37961ea4c3b98b979c"} {"question" "q-98186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-8,\\,4,\\,-1⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/state.json" "file_sha256" "78c771458bf0af71173b6ade2cf888be688e0da9d2268b37961ea4c3b98b979c"} {"question" "q-98211" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate \n${\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{2}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨5,\\,-1,\\,2⟩$\nand\n${\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-2,\\,-4,\\,3⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/state.json" "file_sha256" "78c771458bf0af71173b6ade2cf888be688e0da9d2268b37961ea4c3b98b979c"} {"question" "q-98211" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the adjacent intervals rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{2}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,-1,\\,2⟩-⟨-2,\\,-4,\\,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨7,\\,3,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/state.json" "file_sha256" "78c771458bf0af71173b6ade2cf888be688e0da9d2268b37961ea4c3b98b979c"} {"question" "q-98211" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "be742f513a141cf803ea569247221f898bdc03e6301fb9cba23ca22ad4c28ba0"} {"question" "q-98211" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/state.json" "file_sha256" "78c771458bf0af71173b6ade2cf888be688e0da9d2268b37961ea4c3b98b979c"} {"question" "q-98211" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-3,\\,3,\\,5⟩"] ["math" "⟨3,\\,-3,\\,-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨3,\\,-5,\\,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨7,\\,-5,\\,-5⟩"] ["math" "⟨7,\\,3,\\,-1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/state.json" "file_sha256" "78c771458bf0af71173b6ade2cf888be688e0da9d2268b37961ea4c3b98b979c"} {"question" "q-98211" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨7,\\,3,\\,-1⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/state.json" "file_sha256" "78c771458bf0af71173b6ade2cf888be688e0da9d2268b37961ea4c3b98b979c"} {"question" "q-98264" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate \n${\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{1}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-1,\\,-3,\\,5⟩$\nand\n${\\int }_{2}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨9,\\,-3,\\,-12⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/state.json" "file_sha256" "78c771458bf0af71173b6ade2cf888be688e0da9d2268b37961ea4c3b98b979c"} {"question" "q-98264" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the adjacent intervals rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{1}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{2}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{2}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,-3,\\,5⟩-⟨9,\\,-3,\\,-12⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-10,\\,0,\\,17⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/state.json" "file_sha256" "78c771458bf0af71173b6ade2cf888be688e0da9d2268b37961ea4c3b98b979c"} {"question" "q-98264" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "be742f513a141cf803ea569247221f898bdc03e6301fb9cba23ca22ad4c28ba0"} {"question" "q-98264" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/state.json" "file_sha256" "78c771458bf0af71173b6ade2cf888be688e0da9d2268b37961ea4c3b98b979c"} {"question" "q-98264" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-1,\\,-7,\\,3⟩"] ["math" "⟨-1,\\,0,\\,5⟩"] ["math" "⟨-10,\\,0,\\,17⟩"] ["math" "⟨-10,\\,2,\\,5⟩"] ["math" "⟨7,\\,1,\\,17⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/state.json" "file_sha256" "78c771458bf0af71173b6ade2cf888be688e0da9d2268b37961ea4c3b98b979c"} {"question" "q-98264" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-10,\\,0,\\,17⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/state.json" "file_sha256" "78c771458bf0af71173b6ade2cf888be688e0da9d2268b37961ea4c3b98b979c"} {"question" "q-129178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate \n${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-3,\\,9,\\,6⟩.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/state.json" "file_sha256" "78c771458bf0af71173b6ade2cf888be688e0da9d2268b37961ea4c3b98b979c"} {"question" "q-129178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{1}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-⟨-3,\\,9,\\,6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-9,\\,-6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, applying the scalar multiplication rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot ⟨3,\\,-9,\\,-6⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-3,\\,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/state.json" "file_sha256" "78c771458bf0af71173b6ade2cf888be688e0da9d2268b37961ea4c3b98b979c"} {"question" "q-129178" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "be742f513a141cf803ea569247221f898bdc03e6301fb9cba23ca22ad4c28ba0"} {"question" "q-129178" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/state.json" "file_sha256" "78c771458bf0af71173b6ade2cf888be688e0da9d2268b37961ea4c3b98b979c"} {"question" "q-129178" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-1,\\,0,\\,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨-3,\\,1,\\,2⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,\\,-3,\\,-2⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,\\,3,\\,-2⟩"] ["math" "⟨3,\\,-9,\\,-6⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/state.json" "file_sha256" "78c771458bf0af71173b6ade2cf888be688e0da9d2268b37961ea4c3b98b979c"} {"question" "q-129178" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨1,\\,-3,\\,-2⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/state.json" "file_sha256" "78c771458bf0af71173b6ade2cf888be688e0da9d2268b37961ea4c3b98b979c"} {"question" "q-129287" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that \n${\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=4\\,i-2\\,j+k,$ \n$c=u\\,i-2\\,j-2\\,k,$\nand \n${\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=0,$ what is the value of $u?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/state.json" "file_sha256" "78c771458bf0af71173b6ade2cf888be688e0da9d2268b37961ea4c3b98b979c"} {"question" "q-129287" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The dot product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the dot-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(u\\,i-2\\,j-2\\,k)\\cdot (4\\,i-2\\,j+\\,k) \\\\  & =4u+4-2 \\\\  & =4u+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\cdot f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=0,$ we must have $4u+2=0,$ which means that $u=-\\frac{1}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/state.json" "file_sha256" "78c771458bf0af71173b6ade2cf888be688e0da9d2268b37961ea4c3b98b979c"} {"question" "q-129287" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "be742f513a141cf803ea569247221f898bdc03e6301fb9cba23ca22ad4c28ba0"} {"question" "q-129287" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/state.json" "file_sha256" "78c771458bf0af71173b6ade2cf888be688e0da9d2268b37961ea4c3b98b979c"} {"question" "q-129287" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/state.json" "file_sha256" "78c771458bf0af71173b6ade2cf888be688e0da9d2268b37961ea4c3b98b979c"} {"question" "q-129287" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14072669/state.json" "file_sha256" "78c771458bf0af71173b6ade2cf888be688e0da9d2268b37961ea4c3b98b979c"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2647 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
